.TH TCPCAT 1 "September 2026" "tcpcat" "Network reconnaissance"
.SH NAME
tcpcat \- fast network scanner with an eBPF/AF_XDP engine and CVE correlation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcpcat
.RI [ options ]
.I target
.RI [ target ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tcpcat
is a network reconnaissance engine written in Go, intended for authorized
security assessments and network administration. It performs TCP and UDP
port scanning with host discovery, service and version detection, OS
fingerprinting, and CVE correlation, and writes machine-readable reports.
.PP
Targets may be host names, IP addresses or CIDR ranges. Raw-socket scans
require root privileges or the
.B CAP_NET_RAW
capability.
.PP
On Linux, the optional
.B \-\-ebpf
engine attaches an XDP program at run time and redirects only the replies to
tcpcat's own probes into AF_XDP sockets; all other traffic on the interface
continues through the normal kernel network stack.
.SH OPTIONS
Only the most common options are listed here. Run
.B tcpcat \-\-help
for the complete, authoritative list.
.SS Target and discovery
.TP
.BI \-i " interface"
Network interface to use, bypassing auto-detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-scope\-file " file"
Restrict scanning to the authorized CIDRs, IPs or domains listed in
.IR file .
.TP
.B \-Pn
Skip host discovery and treat every target as online.
.SS Port and scan type
.TP
.BI \-p " ports"
Ports to scan, for example
.B 80,443
or
.BR 1\-1024 .
.TP
.BI \-\-top\-ports " n"
Scan the
.I n
most common ports.
.TP
.B \-sS
TCP SYN scan.
.TP
.B \-sT
TCP connect scan.
.TP
.B \-sU
UDP scan.
.TP
.B \-\-ebpf
Enable the experimental AF_XDP/eBPF engine (Linux only).
.SS Detection
.TP
.B \-sV
Service and version detection.
.TP
.B \-O
Operating-system detection.
.SS Timing and output
.TP
.BI \-T " 0\-5"
Timing template, from slowest and stealthiest to fastest.
.TP
.BI \-\-rate " pps"
Cap on packets per second.
.TP
.BI \-j " file"
Write results to
.I file
as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-sarif " file"
Write findings to
.I file
as SARIF 2.1.0.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-log " file"
Append an audit record, one JSON object per line, to
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-\-baseline " file"
Compare the current scan against a prior JSON report.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan the 1000 most common ports across a subnet:
.B sudo tcpcat \-sS \-\-top\-ports 1000 192.168.1.0/24
.TP
Detect services and export JSON and SARIF for a single host:
.B sudo tcpcat \-sS \-sV \-O \-p 22,80,443 10.0.0.5 \-j report.json \-\-sarif report.sarif
.TP
Run a conservative, scope-limited assessment with an audit log:
.B sudo tcpcat \-\-profile safe\-production \-\-scope\-file scope.txt \-Pn \-sT \-sV \-p 443 \-\-audit\-log audit.jsonl 10.0.0.5
.SH SECURITY
tcpcat is intended solely for systems you own or are explicitly authorized to
test. Unauthorized scanning may be illegal. See
.B /usr/share/doc/tcpcat/SECURITY.md
for the vulnerability-disclosure process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1),
.BR masscan (1)
.PP
Full documentation and source: https://tcpcat.io
